### Transaction history (FR-S-1, M11) and statements. Fake test data only.
# Prerequisites: "customer1: token" in auth.http (or demo.http), and a few transfers or top-ups to list.
# One row per money movement of the caller's wallet: transfers sent and received, top-ups. Amounts are decimal strings.

### customer1: newest first, first page -> 200 {items:[{id, type, status, amount, currency, counterpartyWalletId,
#   note, createdAt}], page 0, size, totalElements, totalPages}
GET {{api}}/api/v1/wallets/me/transactions?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

### customer1: only outgoing transfers in November (yyyy-MM-dd, Asia/Kolkata days, both included), oldest first
GET {{api}}/api/v1/wallets/me/transactions?type=TRANSFER_OUT&from=2026-11-01&to=2026-11-30&sort=createdAt,asc
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

### customer1: keyset pagination for long histories (empty cursor = first slice; always newest first, no page/sort)
# -> 200 {items, size, nextCursor}: no totals; nextCursor is absent on the last slice.
# Pass the returned nextCursor as ?cursor=... to get the next slice.
GET {{api}}/api/v1/wallets/me/transactions?size=10&cursor=
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

> {% if (response.body.nextCursor) client.global.set("history_cursor", response.body.nextCursor); %}

### customer1: the next slice
GET {{api}}/api/v1/wallets/me/transactions?size=10&cursor={{history_cursor}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

### Bad page size -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED (bounds: trustledger.paging)
GET {{api}}/api/v1/wallets/me/transactions?size=100000
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}

### An officer on the customer endpoint -> 403 ACCESS_DENIED
GET {{api}}/api/v1/wallets/me/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{officer1_token}}

### NOT BUILT YET (SPEC §5, README "Not yet built"): monthly PDF statement -> 404 NOT_FOUND today
GET {{api}}/api/v1/wallets/me/statements/2026-11
Authorization: Bearer {{customer1_token}}
